{"nodes": [{"id": "services_segment_requirements_segment_service_deps", "label": "Segment service Python dependency set", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "services/segment/requirements.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "services_segment_requirements_rembg_backend_choice", "label": "rembg onnxruntime backend choice (cpu vs gpu)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "services/segment/requirements.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "rembg needs an explicit backend: rembg[cpu] gives onnxruntime with the CoreML EP on Apple Silicon and works everywhere; rembg[gpu] is CUDA and Linux-only. Default is cpu for cross-platform installs."}, {"id": "services_segment_requirements_optional_dep_degradation", "label": "Optional deps degrade endpoints to 501", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "services/segment/requirements.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "torch/transformers (SAM), Depth and simple-lama-inpainting are each optional: when absent the owning endpoint returns 501 while /segment keeps working, and the Next.js route falls back to HuggingFace SD inpainting."}, {"id": "services_segment_requirements_shared_global_env", "label": "Shared global Python env (no venv) forces version ceilings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "services/segment/requirements.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because both services share one global environment rather than per-service venvs, rembg is capped below 2.0.70 and opencv below 4.11 to keep numpy<2 for sam3."}, {"id": "services_segment_requirements_model_size_tradeoffs", "label": "Model size/quality trade-off notes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "services/segment